From 113383ad66f7cb9925b763c4995e8fb9652b39d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: coop-fw <coop-fw@localhost>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 21:55:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Write traces: --watch-writes logs every PC that stores
 into a range

Emulator::AddWriteTrace(lo, hi, fn) sees every store that lands in a range
after it reached memory, at every width (the per-address write hooks only see
32-bit stores and replace them). The pages it covers leave DirectPages(), so
generated code calls back for each access; bcore materializes CpuState::pc
before every memory callback, so the storing packet PC is readable there.

gui: --watch-writes RANGE (repeatable; LO-HI, LO+LEN or LO, hex) records per
writer PC the store count, nonzero count, widths, address span, first/last
value and guest times, prints each new writer as it appears and a table at
exit (--watch-out FILE for TSV); --watch-log N / --watch-from S print N single
stores from guest time S, which gives the writer order inside a block. Works in
every build, no probe hit cap.
